	(text "AUDIO OUTPUT\nLine level: U59 buffers -> R14/R15 + C103/C104 (AC coupling, 47k bleeders R16/R17) -> LINE_L/LINE_R\n-> J39 LINE OUT (about 0.9 V RMS at full scale) and the amplifier.\nAmplifier: R26/R27 (470k) into RV1 (dual 10k log) attenuate the line level by 34 dB at full volume.\nU89 TDA2822M (stereo, 39 dB fixed gain) runs from +5V through R32/C122 (1R + 1000u, a 160 Hz filter that keeps\nlogic noise out): about 0.25 W per channel into 8 ohm. For more volume from quiet material lower R26/R27 (220k = -27 dB).\nJ18 (3.5 mm, switched): a plug lifts T/R off TN/RN, muting the speaker headers J40/J41.\nHeadphones and external speakers on J18 are driven directly: turn RV1 down before plugging in headphones.\nJ40/J41 (pin 1 speaker, pin 2 GNDA): external 8 ohm mini speakers such as Adafruit 1898 (0.2 W)\nor Kitronik 3316 (0.15 W). R30/R31 (2.2R) hold them to about 0.15 W at full output;\nuse 0R (link) for 0.2 W speakers.\nGrounding: all audio parts return to GNDA. R18 (0R) is the only GNDA-GND tie: place it at U89 pin 4 and\nrun the J18 sleeve, J40/J41 pin 2, the Zobels (C116/C117) and C122/C123 straight to that point.\nDecoupling: C105 at U57, C106 at U58, C107-C110 at U59, C122/C123 at U89 pin 2."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 32.004 134.366 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 0.889 0.889)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
